{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f87e39d99b57bc5b83", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "d and f Block Elements - Test 2", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 37, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250804"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d92507b6", "title": "Chemistry Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d925074c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f45"], "concepts": ["6162fbe46ed13040ec8543bc"], "question": {"text": "The common positive oxidation states for an element with atomic number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo>,</mo></math> are:"}, "options": [{"id": "e85240", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d925074d"}, {"id": "4baa6d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d925074e"}, {"id": "82365d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d925074f"}, {"id": "f47298", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250750"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250751", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b73"], "concepts": ["6162fbe76ed13040ec8545bb"], "question": {"text": "The incorrect statement is:"}, "options": [{"id": "0f9941", "text": "Manganate and permanganate ions are tetrahedral", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250752"}, {"id": "02ac83", "text": "In manganate and permanganate ions, the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></math>-bonding takes place by overlap of p-orbitals of oxygen and d-orbitals of maganese", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250753"}, {"id": "9a928c", "text": "Manganate and permanganate ions are paramagnetic", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250754"}, {"id": "138cc3", "text": "Manganate ion is green in colour and permanganate ion is purple in colour", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250755"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250756", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478a"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b474b"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements:<br/>Statement (I) : In the Lanthanoids, the formation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ce</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></math> is favoured by its noble gas configuration.<br/>Statement (II) : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ce</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></math> is a strong oxidant reverting to the common <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math> state.<br/>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "319f17", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250757"}, {"id": "46c55c", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250758"}, {"id": "484b88", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250759"}, {"id": "66b8ae", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d925075a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d925075b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f45"], "concepts": ["61ab7a186fe44bfe0fe4b93c"], "question": {"text": "Match List - I with List - II.\n\\begin{array}{llll} & List - I & & List - II \\\\(A) & Bronze & (I) &\\mathrm{Cu}, \\mathrm{Ni} \\\\(B) & Brass & (II) &\\mathrm{Fe}, \\mathrm{Cr}, \\mathrm{Ni}, \\mathrm{C} \\\\(C) & UK silver coin & (III) &\\mathrm{Cu}, \\mathrm{Zn} \\\\(D) & Stainless steel & (IV) &\\mathrm{Cu}, \\mathrm{Sn}\\end{array}\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "dd7d26", "text": "(A)-(IV), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(I)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d925075c"}, {"id": "d91bac", "text": "(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(I), (D)-(II)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d925075d"}, {"id": "b22caf", "text": "(A)-(III), (B)-(IV), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d925075e"}, {"id": "6f13c9", "text": "(A)-(III), (B)-(I), (C)-(IV), (D)-(II)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d925075f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250760", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b73"], "concepts": ["60d3035daf049203d853666b"], "question": {"text": "Potassium dichromate acts as a strong oxidizing agent in acidic solution. During this process, the oxidation state changes from"}, "options": [{"id": "264f08", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250761"}, {"id": "e10f13", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250762"}, {"id": "19eb20", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250763"}, {"id": "07d17c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250764"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250765", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478a"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4742"], "question": {"text": "The highest possible oxidation states of uranium and plutonium, respectively, are"}, "options": [{"id": "1f6a4b", "text": "<math><mn>4</mn></math>  and  <math><mn>6</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250766"}, {"id": "69355a", "text": "<math><mn>7</mn></math>  and  <math><mn>6</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250767"}, {"id": "0f84ec", "text": "<math><mn>6</mn></math>  and  <math><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250768"}, {"id": "621f63", "text": "<math><mn>6</mn></math>  and  <math><mn>7</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d9250769"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d925076a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f45"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52be"], "question": {"text": "The metal ion (in gaseous state) with lowest spin-only magnetic moment value is"}, "options": [{"id": "a69237", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d925076b"}, {"id": "055318", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d925076c"}, {"id": "735560", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d925076d"}, {"id": "87a51b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d925076e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f352ee0e063d925076f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b73"], "concepts": ["6162fbe76ed13040ec8545cf"], "question": {"text": "Formulae for Nessler&#39;s reagent is:"}, "options": [{"id": "556b7f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/